markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h2 >What Is a Web App?</h2>

<p >A web app is a program that runs inside a browser like Chrome, Safari, or Edge, rather than being installed on a device. That is exactly what your students will be building in Web Lab: pages that live in the browser and respond to what a user does, instead of static pages that just display information.</p>

<p >Website and web app get used interchangeably a lot, and it is worth drawing the line for your students early. A website, like an online brochure, mostly displays information. A web app lets someone do something: submit a form, play a game, generate text with AI, or draw on a canvas. When a student's project responds to a click instead of just displaying text, that is the shift you are looking for.</p>

<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; width: 95%; margin: 20px auto; padding: 0 5px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/f717660937a4dfe9e5ee5c26c2559e84-image-1760984133668.png" alt="Gmail logo" style="border-radius: 10px; width: 32%;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/1c777228b8b20369dbbd4bdc9c541b32-image-1760984038365.png" alt="Netflix logo" style="border-radius: 10px; width: 32%;">
